TOKEN tinybird_read_public READ
TOKEN tinybird_read READ

DESCRIPTION >
Per-route model health, one row per route actually called for a given
public model. model_health groups by (model, event_type) and collapses
model_used down to a single primary via topKIf(1), which is exactly right
for "did the caller get a response?" but cannot answer "which route served
it?" or "is the primary still alive?" — a model rescued on every request
reads 100% healthy there.

This pipe keeps model_used and model_provider_used as group-by keys instead
of collapsing them, so every fallback route a model has ever fallen through
to gets its own row alongside the primary's. Columns are named identically
to model_health (status_2xx, errors_4xx, errors_5xx, latency_p50_ms, ...) so
consumers can reuse the same health-status computation unchanged: within a
single route's rows, model_used never differs, so no fallback_used filter is
needed to isolate "this route's own" traffic the way model_health's own_calls
must — every row already belongs to exactly one route.
Time window is controlled by the `minutes` parameter (default 60).

NODE model_route_health_stats
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        resolved_model_requested as model,
        event_type,
        model_provider_used as provider,
        model_used,
        -- Constant within a group: a route either always serves as the
        -- model's own primary or always arrives here as a fallback target.
        -- max() just turns the constant into a scalar for the row.
        max(fallback_used) as fallback_used,
        count() as total_requests,
        countIf(response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300) as status_2xx,
        countIf(response_status >= 400 AND response_status < 500) as errors_4xx,
        countIf(response_status >= 500) as errors_5xx,
        -- How many of this route's calls were the one the caller actually
        -- received, as opposed to a call that was retried elsewhere.
        countIf(is_final) as served,
        countIf(
            -- Qualified: the SELECT aliases `fallback_used` to max(fallback_used)
            -- above, and an unqualified reference here would resolve to that
            -- aggregate, which ClickHouse rejects as a nested aggregate.
            is_final AND generation_event_v2.fallback_used
            AND response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300
        ) as fallback_rescues,
        -- A non-final 503 from this route was retried elsewhere. Capacity
        -- pressure, not a caller-visible failure.
        countIf(NOT is_final AND response_status = 503) as primary_retried_503s,
        maxIf(start_time, response_status >= 500) as last_error_at,
        round(quantileIf(0.5)(response_time, response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300), 0) as latency_p50_ms,
        round(quantileIf(0.95)(response_time, response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300), 0) as latency_p95_ms,
        round(avgIf(response_time, response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300), 0) as avg_latency_ms,
        max(start_time) as last_request_at,
        if(
            sumIf(
                response_time,
                response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300
                AND (token_count_completion_text > 0 OR token_count_completion_reasoning > 0)
                AND response_time > 0
            ) > 0,
            round(
                sumIf(
                    toUInt64(token_count_completion_text) + toUInt64(token_count_completion_reasoning),
                    response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300
                    AND (token_count_completion_text > 0 OR token_count_completion_reasoning > 0)
                    AND response_time > 0
                )
                / (
                    sumIf(
                        response_time,
                        response_status >= 200 AND response_status < 300
                        AND (token_count_completion_text > 0 OR token_count_completion_reasoning > 0)
                        AND response_time > 0
                    ) / 1000
                ),
                1
            ),
            NULL
        ) as tokens_per_second
    FROM generation_event_v2
    -- No is_final filter: a route's own health must include the attempts
    -- that were retried elsewhere, not just the one that reached the caller.
    WHERE start_time >= now() - interval {{Int32(minutes, 60)}} minute
    GROUP BY model, event_type, model_used, provider
    ORDER BY model, event_type, total_requests DESC

TYPE endpoint
